      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, the average cost to replace a roof typically ranges from $8,500 to $19,500, with most homeowners paying around $14,800 for a standard 2,000-square-foot home.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "$8,500 to $19,500"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The total investment varies depending on your home's square footage, the pitch (slope) of your roof, and the specific materials you choose to handle Utah\u2019s heavy winters and high-UV summers."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost by Home Size (Asphalt Shingles)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Roofing contractors measure projects by \"squares\" (one 10x10-foot area). For standard architectural asphalt shingles\u2014the most popular option in Utah\u2014the rough breakdown by home size includes full tear-off and installation:"
